  message: "C2 / Phase D/E reorder slice landed: PR #234 (selfh/dev a04ea91b99). BEHAVIORAL EVIDENCE: boundary-node synthesis (create_boundary_nodes + apply_external_id_remap) now runs AFTER tier+noise filtering (Phase E after Phase D), not before. Measured via run_behavior_map on the core package: dangling-src edges 10 -> 0 (2 -> 0 on the gate fixture pkg/foo_pb2.py), edge count unchanged, +1 collapse boundary node, surviving first-party stable_id byte-identical. Production-path gate: packages/hypergumbo-lang-mainstream/tests/test_phase_de_reorder.py (G1 survivor-identity golden, G2 zero-dangling + pb2-import-src-resolved, G3 no-orphans, precondition non-vacuity) RED(2)->GREEN(5) across the reorder. Identity-neutral T0 (no v6 dependency — survivor stable_id unchanged). Adversarial impl review (4 agents, empirical A/B): GO; the one raised MAJOR (supply_chain_summary semantics) was empirically refuted. Tagged awaits_bakeoff_validation (output set membership changes on real repos). SCOPE: C2 only. REMAINING for the full contract / this umbrella: C3 noise-filter entrypoint exemption (entrypoint:F4), C4 total meta relativize (identity:F1), C5 single finalize stage (run-lifecycle:F1), C1 two-pass validation (validator:F3). Item stays OPEN — closes when finalize routing + the serialization round-trip property test land. This reorder UNBLOCKS run-lifecycle:F1 (its R1 entry precondition: substrate final on entry). Design artifact: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/wipozur_phase_de_codesign_06142026.md; D-D carve-out kept as commented no-op."  # 250c
